The project duration is 4 years, with a budget of 3 million euros. Our consortium has experience in similar projects, including digital workplace transformation and AI-powered document management systems. We have expertise in AI, ML, cloud architecture, API integration, data engineering, cybersecurity, and change management.

Our approach includes establishing a steering committee to ensure effective governance, defining the project scope, timeline, and budget during the inception and design phase, and providing regular progress reports to the steering committee. We will also conduct regular security audits and risk assessments to identify and mitigate potential security risks.

We are committed to reducing energetic consumption and relying on infrastructures with low carbon impact. Our solution will contribute to the reduction of the environmental footprint of the City of Belval's information systems, in line with its policy of sustainable development.

In terms of technical capabilities, our company has expertise in large language models, retrieval-augmented generation, and explainability. We use technologies such as containerization with Docker, Kubernetes, and Helm to optimize our solution. Our approach ensures that the generated contents are adapted to the administrative context and comply with quality requirements.

We believe that our comprehensive solution meets the City of Belval's requirements and expectations, providing a high level of relevance and quality to the client. We are confident that our approach will improve the efficiency and quality of service rendered to users by the City of Belval's administrative services, while ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements and reducing environmental footprint.
